= The Constituent Assembly Is Dispersed

On 18 January (5 January, Old Style) the Constituent Assembly met in the Tauride Palace. The Bolsheviks and the Left SRs held about a third of the seats. Viktor Chernov was elected chairman, and the Assembly declined to accept the Bolshevik declaration of the rights of the working people. The Bolsheviks and Left SRs left the hall. At four in the morning the head of the guard, the anarchist sailor Zheleznyakov, told Chernov: "The guard is tired." The deputies went home.

The Assembly has been dissolved by decree. Demonstrations in its support were fired on in Petrograd. A few thousand workers were killed or wounded.

[? if ca_moderate = 1 : The moderate socialists and their allies had the majority, and no armed force to defend it. ?]

- @protest: Protest, and turn to the soviets.
- @provinces: Try to reconvene the Assembly in the provinces. (1 resource)

@protest
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: -3, rel_bol: -3});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 2, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, 3);
!}

We protested in the Soviet and the press. The Assembly is gone. Our work, for now, is in the soviets and the unions, if they will let us.

@provinces
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.add(Q, {repression: 6, rel_bol: -8, soviet_democracy: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 4, middle: 3, workers: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 3, -4);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 6);
Q.reconvene_assembly = 1;
Q.white_aid += 0.5;
!}

A group of delegates left for the Volga to reconvene the Assembly there. It is unlikely that the Bolsheviks will allow it, and equally unlikely that we can stop the delegates from trying.
